Local fix, not an upstream backport. Drop it once php-src fixes this upstream.

PHP 8.6 compiles most of ext/intl as C++. Those files include php.h, whose
main/snprintf.h has `#define vsnprintf ap_php_vsnprintf`, before
<unicode/ucol.h>, which in C++ includes <functional> and through it libc++'s
locale support. On Linux that is __locale_dir/support/linux.h, which calls
std::vsnprintf; the macro turns it into std::ap_php_vsnprintf, and the collator
and grapheme files fail to compile with zig's libc++. GCC's libstdc++ and
macOS's libc++ never reach that call, so upstream CI does not see it.

The macro is set aside only while ucol.h is read, at each place it is first
included after php.h, and restored right after, so PHP's own code still calls
ap_php_vsnprintf. No source token changes outside those headers.

diff --git a/ext/intl/collator/collator_class.h b/ext/intl/collator/collator_class.h
--- a/ext/intl/collator/collator_class.h
+++ b/ext/intl/collator/collator_class.h
@@ -28,7 +28,12 @@
 }
 #endif
 
+/* snprintf.h's vsnprintf macro would rename std::vsnprintf in the libc++
+ * headers ucol.h includes in C++. */
+#pragma push_macro("vsnprintf")
+#undef vsnprintf
 #include <unicode/ucol.h>
+#pragma pop_macro("vsnprintf")
 
 typedef struct {
 	// error handling
